0..75 Comment "// `p then q` moves `p` along `q` in `y. Path(A, a, y)`, and that transport"
76..153 Comment "// appends on its first word whatever `q` is: the empty word is the unit, and"
154..226 Comment "// a letter stays first (#422). Two definitions whose composites are one"
227..295 Comment "// transport, stuck on its two parameters, name one path (#440). The"
296..370 Comment "// composite and its unit laws are the HoTT book\'s Lemmas 2.1.2 and 2.1.4."
372..386 Comment "// The circle."
